class Solution {
    public boolean isSubsequence(String s, String t) {
        
        // If s is empty, it is always a subsequence of t
        if (s.length() == 0)
            return true;

        // i -> pointer for string s
        // j -> pointer for string t
        int i = 0, j = 0;

        // Traverse both strings
        // Stop when either string is fully traversed
        while (i < s.length() && j < t.length()) {

            // If characters match, move both pointers
            if (s.charAt(i) == t.charAt(j)) {
                i++;   // move in s
                j++;   // move in t
            } 
            else {
                // If not match, only move pointer in t
                // because we are trying to find s inside t
                j++;
            }
        }

        // If we have matched all characters of s,
        // then s is a subsequence of t
        return i == s.length();
    }
}
⏱️ Time Complexity

You traverse t at most once

s is also traversed once (via pointer i)

👉 Time Complexity = O(n + m)

n = s.length()

m = t.length()

Since m can be up to 
10
4
10
4
, this is efficient.

🧠 Space Complexity

No extra data structures used

Only a few variables (i, j)

👉 Space Complexity = O(1) (constant space)
